2Ki 24:1 , Jehoiakim, first subdued by Nebuchadnezzar, then rebelling against him, procures his own ruin;
2Ki 24:5 , Jehoiachin succeeds him;
2Ki 24:7 , The king of Egypt is vanquished by the king of Babylon;
2Ki 24:8 , Jehoiachin's evil reign;
2Ki 24:10 , Jerusalem is taken and carried captive into Babylon;
2Ki 24:17 , Zedekiah is made king, and reigns ill, unto the utter destruction of Judah.
